cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Herald in research or a product, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Herald: a local-first communication agent"
abstract: >-
  Herald is a local-first communication agent written in Rust. It reads
  connected communication providers, summarizes and drafts with a local model,
  and performs outbound actions only after an explicit policy check and a
  human approval. The model emits a typed plan; Rust validates, authorizes, and
  executes it, and every write is idempotent and reconciled when its outcome is
  uncertain. Herald ships a deterministic fake provider and a Maildir provider
  with SMTP submission, stores state in local SQLite, and keeps inference local
  by default.
authors:
